- Read /ai-context before major changes
- Keep UI thin
- Backend owns all calculations, frontend is pure display
- Do not create duplicate pages if existing pages can be upgraded
- Preserve existing API compatibility
- Use TypeScript types
- Use FastAPI response models
- Follow dark trading dashboard style
- Use CSS custom properties for theme tokens. Light/dark themes defined via CSS variables in `:root`/`html.dark`/`html.light`. Tailwind classes (`bg-gray-900`, etc.) auto-adapt. Adding a new color? Check `/frontend/src/index.css` theme tokens first.
- Use `color-mix()` for alpha variants instead of hardcoding opacity values
- Use semantic theme tokens : `bg-surface-card`, `text-text-primary`, `border-border-subtle` when possible from tailwind.config.js
- Use badges, cards, expandable rows
- Avoid clutter
- Never auto‑execute real trades
- Paper trade or human approval only
